id: pm-web-f9r8
title: Ecosystem release readiness pass 2026-07-06
description: "July 6, 2026 fleet readiness pass for the pm package ecosystem."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: agent-audit,context-management,ecosystem,release-readiness
created_at: "2026-07-06T15:33:35.399Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-27T23:17:21.300Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-27T23:04:15.921Z"
author: codex
acceptance_criteria: Package uses current pm CLI/SDK and pm-changelog; release/check scripts pass; pm items capture decisions; no tracked secrets/private data are introduced; GitHub PR/release state is reviewed.
release: 2026.7.10
resolution: Work completed and released in 2026.7.10. Release attribution set explicitly so pm-changelog --respect-item-release files the entry under 2026.7.10 instead of the current release notes.
expected_result: "A closed item whose changelog entry appears under the 2026.7.10 heading it actually shipped in, leaving the current release notes untouched."
actual_result: "Before this closeout the item had remained in_progress with no activity since its work shipped, so the delivery was missing from the changelog while still being counted as open work in every fleet audit. Closing it with an explicit release attribution is what added the historical entry."
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-10T04:38:21.982Z",codex,"Functional review found a real defect: src/server.ts never mounted createApp() — legal routes/308 aliases existed only in the tested app factory while the running server kept its own duplicated route stack (catch-all SPA served 200 for every path, /impressum did not redirect). Fixed by rewriting server.ts to consume createApp() and keep only DB init + listen + SSE cleanup. Verified live against throwaway Postgres: /legal-notice serves standalone page, /impressum 308->/legal-notice, healthz + SPA fallback + cookie-consent.js intact. 46/46 tests, changelog:check green, npm audit 0 vulns."
close_reason: "Retired as shipped: the ecosystem release readiness pass of 2026-07-06 was completed and released in 2026.7.10, but the item was never closed and sat in progress ever since, inflating every fleet audit."
body: "Track the July 6, 2026 fleet pass: align package metadata with latest pm CLI/SDK and pm-changelog, verify daily release automation, run build/test/audit/package checks with real workspace data where practical, inspect GitHub state, and record privacy/history findings without changing pm-cli itself."
